meta {
  name: 66 Attachments
  seq: 66
}

docs {
  # Attachments (generic)

  A polymorphic attachment sub-resource (`attachments` module). Any feature can
  persist an uploaded file's S3 URL against one of its records via
  (`entityType`, `entityId`) — no per-feature table needed. Bytes are uploaded
  first via **65 Uploads → Upload Attachment** (returns `{ url }`); this module
  then records that URL + metadata.

  Endpoints (all under `/attachments`, business-authenticated, tenant + active
  branch from the JWT):
  - `POST /attachments` — attach a file to an owner record
  - `GET /attachments?entityType=&entityId=&category=` — list an owner's files
  - `DELETE /attachments/:id` — soft-delete

  `entityType` is an allow-listed slug (INCIDENT_REPORT, TECHNICIAN_PROCESS,
  QUALITY_CONTROL, INVENTORY, ACCESSION, TEMPLATE, ORDER, PATIENT, LAB_REPORT,
  PHLEBOTOMY, MISC). Run **Business Auth → Login** first.
}
